    # Source: Adventure Guide - The Exorcism of Mikko (Badwolf Studios; Chase McAllister
    # and Jake Rafter), pages 2 and 13-14. An adventure set in Axis, so it layers on the
    # Axis preview core (which itself EXTENDS the D&D 2024 SRD 5.2.1 base); nothing in
    # either parent is edited. Base spells the adventure alters are widened here with
    # MODIFY … PROPERTIES so the alteration is a typed field on the spell, not a note.
    # Every DESCRIPTION / TEXT is verbatim source text.
    # ============= Types this adventure introduces / widens =============
    # The adventure's NPC boxes: an epithet line, a line of comma-separated traits, and
    # a paragraph or two. Nested in the character's PROFILES block (a character with a
    # stat block is one DEF; its boxes are its profiles - "Adam Taylor" and
    # "Adam Taylor, Possessed" are two boxes about one creature).
    #tE0aKgaFAGyt83vTPEsS3tU ^"NPC Profile" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Epithet" STRING
            ^"Traits" LIST OF STRING
            ^"Description" STRING
        }
    }
    # 2014-style stat blocks: an AC parenthetical, a printed legendary-action budget, and
    # prepared-spell lists by slot level.
    # ============= The Cult of Orcus (page 2, text box) =============
    #toQrCRTjquufY8PmpxGJMzZ ^"The Cult of Orcus" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Kind" STRING "Apostate Organization"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "A secretive group burrowed deep in many societies all throughout Axis, Mikko is no exception. Adherents of the profane religion of the Lord of Silence occasionally are not even aware that they act in the service of that Dread Beast.

Fully rooting out the cult is a nearly impossible task, as any person could be a member, knowingly or not. Even more so in places like Mikko, where one of the Undead King’s heralds is even now operating invisibly.

Many actions during this adventure can be blamed directly on cult activities. Corruption inflicted by the Cult of Orcus often manifests as a soft buzzing at the edge of hearing progressing into an aversion to loud noises and light."
    }
    # ============= Special Rules for the Exorcism (pages 13-14) =============
    #twO58ybgoJo25TONy2At7M2 ^"Corruption" DEF {
        OPTIONAL {
            DEFAULT off
            SCOPE GLOBAL
            TEXT "An optional rule for a more harrowing playstyle, the player characters may be able to be brought low by exposure to the corrupting influence of the horrors of the world."
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Whenever a character encounters a corruptive influence for the first time, they must test against corruption. These encounters could be anything, whether that’s reading from particularly twisted tome written in the blood of a fallen Celestial, the act of witnessing the veil of reality being torn asunder, or encountering a specific horrifying monster. Subsequent encounters with similar events do not force a corruption test, unless they are particularly harrowing.

When testing against corruption, a player rolls 1d20. If the roll is 10 or higher, they succeed. If they fail, they gain one point of corruption, up to a maximum of five. A character with any points of corruption is considered to be corrupted.

Once per day, as a part of a short rest, a character with corruption may attempt to center themselves and reduce their corruption rating instead of regaining hit points. The character re-attempts their test against corruption, this time adding their Wisdom modifier to the roll. If the result is 10 or higher, they succeed, and their corruption score is reduced by one. A casting of lesser restoration grants a character advantage on this roll.

Particularly potent spells such as greater restoration, and resurrection may remove all points of corruption on a corrupted individual."
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Maximum Points" INTEGER 5
            ^"Test" DEF {
                ^"Die" STRING "1d20"
                ^"Success Threshold" INTEGER 10
                ^"Failure" STRING "gain one point of corruption"
            }
            ^"Centering" DEF {
                ^"Frequency" STRING "Once per day, as a part of a short rest"
                ^"Cost" STRING "instead of regaining hit points"
                ^"Modifier" STRING "Wisdom modifier"
                ^"Success Threshold" INTEGER 10
                ^"Success" STRING "corruption score is reduced by one"
                ^"Advantage From" LIST OF STRING ["Lesser Restoration"]
            }
            ^"Removed Entirely By" LIST OF STRING ["Greater Restoration", "Resurrection"]
        }
        REFERENCES {
            "lesser restoration" -> #tN4xsLRODhZ7EYM0WBqywbpU ^"Lesser Restoration"
            "greater restoration" -> #tHeb9fNGKnVq9j95vHfasRbv ^"Greater Restoration"
        }
    }
    #taNWD1OX1B2qTkg1B0aG7zN ^"Corrupted" DEF {
        EXTENDS ^"Condition"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Description" STRING "Creatures who are corrupted can have between one and five points of corruption, with compounding effects based on the number of points of corruption. Creatures with fewer than 6 Intelligence cannot become corrupted. While you have the corrupted condition, you experience the following effects.

**Dissociation.** You have a harder time parsing the world around you and interacting with it. For every point of corruption you have, you suffer a cumulative -1 penalty on ability checks, attack rolls, and saving throws.

**Debilitating Madness.** Creatures with five points of corruption no longer gain the benefits of a long rest, treating any such activity as a short rest instead. Additionally, a creature with five points of corruption gains one point of exhaustion every six hours.

**Possession Vulnerability.** If you have three or more points of corruption, you suffer disadvantage to resist possession effects.

**Unnerving Presence.** Corrupted characters can be recognized by those looking for the signs. A successful Insight check (Difficulty 15 - points of corruption) can recognize a corrupt individual."
            ^"Points" DEF {
                ^"Min" INTEGER 1
                ^"Max" INTEGER 5
            }
            ^"Minimum Intelligence" INTEGER 6
        }
        EFFECTS {
            ^"Dissociation" DEF {
                ^"Description"
                STRING "You have a harder time parsing the world around you and interacting with it. For every point of corruption you have, you suffer a cumulative -1 penalty on ability checks, attack rolls, and saving throws."
                ^"Penalty Per Point"
                INTEGER -1
                ^"Applies To"
                LIST OF STRING ["ability checks", "attack rolls", "saving throws"]
            }
            ^"Debilitating Madness" DEF {
                ^"Description"
                STRING "Creatures with five points of corruption no longer gain the benefits of a long rest, treating any such activity as a short rest instead. Additionally, a creature with five points of corruption gains one point of exhaustion every six hours."
                ^"At Points"
                INTEGER 5
                ^"Exhaustion Interval Hours"
                INTEGER 6
            }
            ^"Possession Vulnerability" DEF {
                ^"Description"
                STRING "If you have three or more points of corruption, you suffer disadvantage to resist possession effects."
                ^"At Points"
                INTEGER 3
            }
            ^"Unnerving Presence" DEF {
                ^"Description"
                STRING "Corrupted characters can be recognized by those looking for the signs. A successful Insight check (Difficulty 15 - points of corruption) can recognize a corrupt individual."
                ^"Check" DEF {
                    ^"Skill"
                    STRING "Insight"
                    ^"DC"
                    STRING "15 - points of corruption"
                }
            }
        }
    }
    REFERENCES {
        "corrupted condition" -> #taNWD1OX1B2qTkg1B0aG7zN ^"Corrupted"
    }
    # Source: Adventure Guide - The Exorcism of Mikko, page 15 ("New Spells").
    # Same shape as the SRD spells (dnd5.5e-0.4-spells.ttrpg) plus the ^"Tradition"
    # field the rules file introduces ("Sangromancy", printed after the school).
    #tTdSt1Y1WpI6CbIZY484Fx8 ^"Boiling Blood" DEF {
        EXTENDS ^"Spell"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Level" INTEGER 3
            ^"School" STRING "Transmutation"
            ^"Tradition" STRING "Sangromancy"
            ^"Casting Time" STRING "Action"
            ^"Range" STRING "Personal"
            ^"Components" STRING "V"
            ^"Duration" STRING "1 hour"
            ^"Description" STRING "The caster ignites the soul present in their vital fluids, making them burn like fire. The caster must sacrifice a number of hit dice to fuel the power of this spell, minimum one.

The caster gains an unarmed melee attack in which they are proficient. This unarmed attack counts as a finesse weapon, and deals Xd6 fire damage, where X is the number of hit dice sacrificed to fuel this spell. Additionally, if the caster is dealt damage by a piercing or slashing attack from five feet or less, the attacker must attempt a Dexterity Saving throw or take X fire damage- the caster automatically takes half of this damage, before calculating resistances."
            ^"Classes" LIST OF STRING ["Bard", "Sorcerer", "Wizard", "Warlock"]
            ^"Sacrifice" DEF {
                ^"Resource" STRING "Hit Dice"
                ^"Minimum" INTEGER 1
            }
            ^"Unarmed Attack" DEF {
                ^"Finesse" BOOLEAN true
                ^"Damage Dice Per Hit Die Sacrificed" STRING "1d6"
                ^"Damage Type" STRING "Fire"
            }
            ^"Retribution" DEF {
                ^"Trigger" STRING "dealt damage by a piercing or slashing attack from five feet or less"
                ^"Save" DEF {
                    ^"Ability" STRING "Dexterity"
                }
                ^"Damage" STRING "X fire damage"
                ^"X" STRING "the number of hit dice sacrificed to fuel this spell"
                ^"Caster Takes" STRING "half of this damage, before calculating resistances"
            }
        }
    }
    #tLclfbAMrzrJTSxrUVBDXF1 ^"Sieve of the Animus" DEF {
        EXTENDS ^"Spell"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Level" INTEGER 2
            ^"School" STRING "Abjuration"
            ^"Tradition" STRING "Sangromancy"
            ^"Casting Time" STRING "Action"
            ^"Range" STRING "30 feet"
            ^"Components" STRING "V, S"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Instantaneous"
            ^"Description" STRING "By tapping into the magic of their own blood, the caster can cleanse spiritual impurities from another.

The caster must sacrifice a number of Hit Dice to fuel the power of this spell, minimum one. If a number of hit dice have been spent equal or greater than the highest spell level affecting the target, or the charisma modifier of the possessing spirit, whichever is higher, the effects of this spell are increased.

The target attempts a Wisdom saving throw. If the target fails, and enough hit dice have been sacrificed, the target is cleansed of spiritual possession, as well as of the charmed and frightened conditions. The target is then stunned for a number of rounds equal to the number of hit dice sacrificed. If not enough hit dice have been sacrificed, the target is only stunned for a number of rounds equal to the number of hit dice sacrificed.

If the target succeeds at their Wisdom Saving throw and enough hit dice have been sacrificed, the target is stunned for a number of rounds equal to the number of hit dice sacrificed. If not enough hit dice have been sacrificed, there is no effect.

A target stunned by this spell may attempt a new Wisdom saving throw at the end of their turn to end the effect early."
            ^"Classes" LIST OF STRING ["Bard", "Cleric", "Druid", "Paladin", "Ranger", "Sorcerer", "Wizard", "Warlock"]
            ^"Sacrifice" DEF {
                ^"Resource" STRING "Hit Dice"
                ^"Minimum" INTEGER 1
                ^"Threshold" STRING "equal or greater than the highest spell level affecting the target, or the charisma modifier of the possessing spirit, whichever is higher"
            }
            ^"Save" DEF {
                ^"Ability" STRING "Wisdom"
            }
            ^"Outcomes" DEF {
                ^"Failed Save, Enough Hit Dice" STRING "the target is cleansed of spiritual possession, as well as of the charmed and frightened conditions. The target is then stunned for a number of rounds equal to the number of hit dice sacrificed."
                ^"Failed Save, Not Enough Hit Dice" STRING "the target is only stunned for a number of rounds equal to the number of hit dice sacrificed."
                ^"Successful Save, Enough Hit Dice" STRING "the target is stunned for a number of rounds equal to the number of hit dice sacrificed."
                ^"Successful Save, Not Enough Hit Dice" STRING "there is no effect."
            }
            ^"Conditions Removed" LIST OF STRING ["Charmed", "Frightened"]
        }
        REFERENCES {
            "stunned" -> #tc1WFC9wrQqC6gPJzlGzUWlg ^"Stunned"
            "charmed" -> #tT5DRcEfc8g6Q2YAC6JOzbih ^"Charmed"
            "frightened" -> #tAFqlyLL4VPdt1ogtcNozAW8 ^"Frightened"
        }
    }
    # Source: Adventure Guide - The Exorcism of Mikko, page 16 ("Items").
    # SRD ^"Magic Item" shape plus the ^"Cost" (^"Item Cost": Amount + Unit) that the
    # Axis preview core adds - the printed price is "5,000gp", so Amount 5000, Unit "gp".
    #tHxExwUdbujdQ41jj9oR81S ^"Imperial Seal" DEF {
        EXTENDS ^"Magic Item"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Item Type" STRING "Wondrous Item"
            ^"Rarity" STRING "Very Rare"
            ^"Cost" DEF {
                ^"Amount" INTEGER 5000
                ^"Unit" STRING "gp"
            }
            ^"Description" STRING "This Rosette is inscribed with the official Seal of the Empress and bears a unique enchantment to identify the bearer as operating in accordance with the Empresses will. Attempting to sell or forge an Imperial Seal is considered a high crime, on par with treason. A character brandishing this seal"
        }
    }
    #tGgaWi6qJoWBW1ZL6rapVk8 ^"Ravenscroll" DEF {
        EXTENDS ^"Magic Item"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Item Type" STRING "Wondrous Item"
            ^"Rarity" STRING "Common"
            ^"Cost" DEF {
                ^"Amount" INTEGER 15
                ^"Unit" STRING "gp"
            }
            ^"Description" STRING "Not all residents of the Empire are blessed with the ability to perform magic or communicate across long distances. The solution, as devised by the Enchanter’s Guild of Axis, are these clever sheets of paper, with wax seals attached.

A message of up to 280 characters can be inscribed on the sheet, along with a destination. Once inscribed, the wax seal is broken, and the paper folds itself into an animate raven which takes wing to the inscribed destination at supernatural speeds. A Ravenscroll can cover the length of the continent in a single night."
            ^"Message Length" INTEGER 280
        }
    }
    #tWxJtGqnuXMI7uiUpQvSH0q ^"Censer of the Sol Warden" DEF {
        EXTENDS ^"Magic Item"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Item Type" STRING "Wondrous Item"
            ^"Printed Item Type" STRING "Wonderous Item"
            ^"Rarity" STRING "Very Rare"
            ^"Cost" DEF {
                ^"Amount" INTEGER 4750
                ^"Unit" STRING "gp"
            }
            ^"Requires Attunement" BOOLEAN true
            ^"Attunement Requirement" STRING "by a character who is Faithful to the Sol Warden"
            ^"Description" STRING "A golden censor, inscribed with Celestial symbols detailing the protections granted by the Sol Warden.

When sanctified incense is burned within the censor, every character within a 60 ft radius gains advantage on checks and saves made to prevent possession. Further, if an exorcism attempt is made within the affected area, any rolls to accomplish it are made at advantage, rolls to resist are made at disadvantage, and any hit die costs incurred by the exorcist are reduced by two. Incense burned in this censer does not last long; a full censer burns out in one minute."
            ^"Radius" INTEGER 60
            ^"Duration" STRING "one minute"
            ^"Hit Die Cost Reduction" INTEGER 2
        }
        REFERENCES {
            "possession" -> #tzyaMM4LALHld6QPEKqvPHt ^"Possession"
        }
    }
    # Source: Adventure Guide - The Exorcism of Mikko, pages 22, 26-27 ("NPCs and Enemies").
